```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"sync"
)

func WorkerPool(jobs <-chan int, n int) {
	var wg sync.WaitGroup

	worker := func(id int) {
		defer wg.Done()
		for job := range jobs {
			// Process the job here
			fmt.Printf("worker %d processing job %d\n", id, job)
		}
	}

	wg.Add(n)
	for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
		go worker(i)
	}

	wg.Wait()
}
```

### How it works
- `jobs` is a read-only channel of `int` jobs.
- `n` workers are started as goroutines.
- Each worker loops over `jobs` until the channel is closed.
- A `sync.WaitGroup` waits for all workers to finish.

### Example usage
```go
